Preserve the original signed-WORD debris translation after camera rotation.

Update_Debris@0x424640 rotates its relative position using FUN_00413b8e.
At 0x42485c/0x424862/0x424868 the original loads unaligned DWORDs from
0x74c4fe/0x74c502/0x74c506 and then sar ...,16. Their high words are the
low words of the rotated x/y/z at 0x74c500/0x74c504/0x74c508. The following
stores at 0x424876/0x42487c/0x424882 therefore sign-extend those WORDs into
the translation vector. The decompile incorrectly retained each full int.

Observed in the complete unmodified L5 recording at cf546/ticks1094:
debris slot 116 (primitive 0x778110) has matching positions, vertices and
camera matrix. Rotated z reaches -32775; original translation wraps to
32761 while the port's negative depth culls the primitive. Since particle
depth cueing uses the last global __otz, this also changes smoke shades
from 126 to 101 and causes visible differences at cf547..549. Match the
actual integer conversion; inject no state or pixel and change no renderer.

